{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/671384-where-does-the-scar-get-its-spirits","id":671384,"title":"Where does the Scar get its spirits?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-19T15:53:33-07:00","id":671384,"title":"Where does the Scar get its spirits?","content":"We hear about how the Scar constantly processes massive numbers of fetishes for Malfeas, and have even stripped Incarna of their entire broods. I would normally have thought they were just pulling these spirits out of the Abyss, but if they can go after the broods of presumably active Incarna, then I am confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T16:01:17-07:00","id":671401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/671384-where-does-the-scar-get-its-spirits#post671384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We hear about how the Scar constantly processes massive numbers of fetishes for Malfeas, and have even stripped Incarna of their entire broods. I would normally have thought they were just pulling these spirits out of the Abyss, but if they can go after the broods of presumably active Incarna, then I am confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good question, where is it referenced?<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;massive numbers&quot; is most certainly hyperbole - if anything in the cosmos could produce fetishes by the thousands per year (what by comparison is small fry to many actual weapons factory), the garou and other shapeshifters would have been boned decades ago... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T17:05:01-07:00","id":671493,"title":"","content":"I would assume they get them from practically everywhere - anywhere a Bane or Black Spiral manages to trap a spirit, they can move them to Scar and presumably get a little (or not so little, depending on the spirit) bounty paid out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T18:01:29-07:00","id":671549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/671384-where-does-the-scar-get-its-spirits?p=671493#post671493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would assume they get them from practically everywhere - anywhere a Bane or Black Spiral manages to trap a spirit, they can move them to Scar and presumably get a little (or not so little, depending on the spirit) bounty paid out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does make things simpler that, Scar simply processing what other wyrm agents in several fronts send towards it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T15:44:21-07:00","id":672416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/671384-where-does-the-scar-get-its-spirits?p=671401#post671401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good question, where is it referenced?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Page 74 of the new Umbra book. Right at the Monkeywrench section. And it says &quot;No shortage of spirits find the Scar antithetical to their continued purpose. Countless Incarna have lost their brood to the Wyrm-fetish assembly lines of the unforgiving Near Realm. &quot; Hmm... It says brood, and it sounds like brood in its entirety, but I suppose it could be interpreted differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T16:28:33-07:00","id":672468,"title":"","content":"I'd say it's either hyperbole or not meant to mean &quot;the <i>entire</i> brood&quot;. Reading it as entire broods would be the most correct interpretation from a purely semantic point of view, but as we've never heard of even a single Incarna with a brood that has been deported to Scar, I don't think that's what the author meant. Or should have meant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T22:05:47-07:00","id":672888,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... I don't know. I mean, the universe IS a big place, and if every bane in the outer solar system... Nope, I still can't find a rationale. Malfeas IS a big place, and it's security is supposed to be second to none, but that still doesn't explain where all of these fetishes are being put to use. Can anyone think of a rationale? I can imagine minor Incarna losing their broods if there were only a small handful of spirits subordinate to them, but where do they go? And it would be interesting to see some sample fetishes produced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T15:42:28-07:00","id":673484,"title":"","content":"Consider that not all Fetishes are actually Fetishes as items that you buy with points. You cannot really make a Fetish as we know them without binding it into the real world. Even the fetishes made from parts of spiritual creatures need to be stabilised and forged into something useful. Most of the items crafted in the Umbra are explicitly meant for Spirits, and the products of the Scar could be anything, from horrifying serrated blades fused to the skins of former tree spirits, long needle fingers mounted on the hands of pain spirits or giant war machines and strange bane generators. All of these could be a reasonable explanation for what these fetishes are and where they go.<br /> <br /> Now, actually making fetishes in the Umbra, the ones truly crafted their by beings that could bridge the gap between worlds. Now, those are the makings of stories of legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}